From: godotjs
Subject: [godotjs] abseil: link CoreFoundation on the iOS build as well

Anything that links abseil needs CoreFoundation: absl::time_internal::local_time_zone
calls CFTimeZoneCopyDefault, CFStringGetCString and friends. The only place that
framework was named is xcode_settings.OTHER_LDFLAGS, and gyp's ninja generator turns
xcode_settings into flags for the mac flavour only (tools/gyp/pylib/gyp/generator/
ninja.py: `if self.flavor == "mac"`). With --dest-os=ios the flavour is ios, so the
framework was never passed and the first binary to link abseil stopped:

  Undefined symbols for architecture arm64:
    "_CFTimeZoneCopyDefault", referenced from:
        absl::time_internal::cctz::local_time_zone() in libabseil.a[108](...)

Naming the framework under libraries reaches every flavour, and only iOS is added -
macOS keeps getting it from xcode_settings, so macOS link lines do not change at all.
An iOS build's host tools report OS=="ios" the same way its target does, which is what
puts the framework on torque's link line too; that was read back out of the generated
files (out/Release/obj.host/tools/v8_gypfiles/torque.ninja) rather than assumed.
diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
index 1a1de33..8eed247 100644
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/abseil.gyp
@@ -15,6 +15,20 @@
         'xcode_settings': {
           'OTHER_LDFLAGS': ['-framework CoreFoundation'],
         },
+        # Linking abseil needs CoreFoundation: absl::time_internal::cctz::local_time_zone
+        # calls CFTimeZoneCopyDefault, CFStringGetCString and friends. The line above only
+        # reaches the linker for gyp's mac flavour (its ninja generator guards the whole
+        # xcode_settings path with `if self.flavor == "mac"`), so an iOS build - flavour
+        # ios - linked abseil without the framework and stopped with "Undefined symbols
+        # for architecture arm64: _CFTimeZoneCopyDefault, ...". Naming the framework under
+        # libraries is read by every flavour, and an iOS build's host tools report
+        # OS=="ios" too, so the build-time programs (torque first) are covered by this as
+        # well.
+        'conditions': [
+          [ 'OS=="ios"', {
+            'libraries': [ '-framework CoreFoundation' ],
+          }],
+        ],
       },
       'include_dirs': [
         '<(ABSEIL_ROOT)',
